              ":question/id": "05942b5f-c165-59c6-8b67-24bc8dd40cca",
              ":question/math-academy-id": "e-4685",
              ":question/problem": "What would be the system of equations for the following augmented matrix?\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}5 & -4 & -12 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$",
              ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix consists of two parts: the coefficient matrix and the column of constants.\n\nThe coefficient matrix represents the coefficients in the linear system, while the column of constants represents the constants on the right-hand sides of the equations.\n\nUsing the variables $x$ and $y,$ then, the corresponding system of equations is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x-4y &=-12 \\\\ 3x+y &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"
            },
